psusennes-ii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Psusennes II</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Psusennes II was the last king of the Twenty-first Dynasty of Egypt, reigning in the mid-10th century BCE.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/psychoanalysis"><span class="enc-name">Psychoanalysis</span><span class="enc-type">Religion / idea</span><span class="enc-snip">Psychoanalysis is a theory and method of treating mental disorders through the investigation of unconscious processes, developed by Sigmund Freud.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/psychological-warfare"><span class="enc-name">Psychological warfare</span><span class="enc-type">Term</span><span class="enc-snip">Psychological warfare is the use of fear, deception and propaganda to weaken an enemy's will to resist.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/psylli"><span class="enc-name">Psylli</span><span class="enc-type">People / group</span><span class="enc-snip">The Psylli were an ancient Libyan people living on the shores of the Gulf of Sirte in present-day Libya.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ptoion"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ptoion.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ptoion</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Ptoion was a sanctuary of Apollo Ptoios on Mount Ptoon in Boeotia, near the city of Acraephia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/ptolemaeus-of-commagene"><span class="enc-name">Ptolemaeus of Commagene</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ptolemaeus was the founder of the kingdom of Commagene in south-eastern Anatolia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ptolemaic-kingdom"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ptolemaic-kingdom.jpg" al