emy VIII and his sister-wife Cleopatra II.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-viii-physcon"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ptolemy-viii-physcon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ptolemy VIII Physcon</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ptolemy VIII, nicknamed Physcon, was a Ptolemaic king who quarrelled for decades with his brother Ptolemy VI.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/ptolemy-xii-auletes"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ptolemy-xii-auletes.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Ptolemy XII Auletes</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Ptolemy XII Auletes was king of Ptolemaic Egypt from 80 to 58 BCE and again from 55 to 51 BCE, and father of Cleopatra VII.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/pua-district"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pua-district.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Pua district</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Pua is a district in the upper Nan valley of Nan Province in northern Thailand.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/puabi"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/puabi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Puabi</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Puabi was a queen or noblewoman of Ur around 2600 BCE, known from her richly furnished tomb in the Royal Cemetery, excavated by Leonard Woolley in 1927–1928.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/publius-canidius-crassus"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/publius-canidius-crassus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Publius Can