nasarovar and Mount…</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/purdil-khan"><span class="enc-name">Purdil Khan</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Purdil Khan was the eldest of the Kandahar Sardars, Barakzai brothers who took Kandahar after the Durrani Empire broke up in 1818.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/purepecha-empire"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/purepecha-empire.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Purépecha Empire</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Purépecha Empire, also called the Tarascan state, was a powerful polity in western Mexico centred on Lake Pátzcuaro.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/purgatorio"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/purgatorio.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Purgatorio</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">Purgatorio is the second part of Dante Alighieri's Divine Comedy, written in the early 14th century.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/purificacion-uruguay"><span class="enc-name">Purificación (Uruguay)</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Purificación was the settlement founded by José Gervasio Artigas in 1815 on a plateau above the Uruguay river at Hervidero, north of Paysandú.</span></a></li></ul>
